id: 32
hanzi: 馒头
pinyin: mán tou
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: steamed bun; mantou; Chinese plain steamed bread (without filling)
  es: panecillo al vapor; mantou; pan chino tradicional al vapor sin relleno

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a staple food of northern China made of leavened wheat flour dough shaped into rounded loaves and steamed, typically without sweet or savory filling | bollo de masa de harina de trigo fermentada cocido al vapor sin relleno, básico en el norte de China | 热气腾腾的馒头 (steaming hot mantou / piping hot steamed buns)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 清晨的集市上，蒸笼盖刚一揭开，一股浓郁的麦香伴着滚滚白汽扑面而来，白白胖胖的馒头格外诱人。 | Qīngchén de jíshì shàng, zhēnglóng gài gāng yì jiēkāi, yì gǔ nóngyù de màixiāng bàn zhe gǔngǔn báiqì pūmiàn'érlái, báibái-pàngpàng de mántou géwài yòurén. | In the morning market, as the steamer lid lifted, rich wheat aromas poured forth with billowing white steam, revealing irresistible plump white mantou. | En el mercado matinal, al levantar la tapa de la vaporera brotó un denso vaho de trigo; los panecillos blancos y esponjosos resultaban tentadores.
  #2 | 在我国北方传统饮食文化中，暄软劲道的老面馒头不仅是日常三餐的充饥主食，也是承载乡愁的味觉记忆。 | Zài wǒguó běifāng chuántǒng yǐnshí wénhuà zhōng, xuānruǎn jìndao de lǎomiàn mántou bùjǐn shì rìcháng sāncān de chōngjī zhǔshí, yě shì chéngzài xiāngchóu de wèijué jìyì. | In northern Chinese cuisine, soft and chewy traditional sourdough mantou is not just a staple, but a sensory embodiment of hometown nostalgia. | En la cocina tradicional del norte de China, el panecillo al vapor de masa madre no es solo alimento diario, sino la memoria afectiva del hogar.

