character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  馒 | mán | steamed bread / mantou | panecillo al vapor | 饣 | food / eat | 饣 (steamed food dough) | 曼 (màn, graceful / stretch) | 14 | 左右结构 | Simplified from 饅. Phono-semantic character where food radical 饣 signifies leavened grain dough, and 曼 supplies sound. | Kneaded wheat dough (饣) stretched and rolled out smoothly (曼) before being placed in high steam baskets makes fluffy steamed buns (馒). | La masa de harina (饣) estirada y moldeada con primor (曼) que esponja en la vaporera da lugar al tierno panecillo (馒). | 35 | NVAWE | 饅
  头 | tóu | head; top; chief; suffix | cabeza; cima; principal; sufijo | 大 | big / head | 一 (crown of head) | 八/大 (human body) | 5 | 单一结构 | Simplified from 頭. Ancient bronze character depicted a human neck and cranial head with hair on top, now serving as head and nominal noun suffix. | A human neck supporting a round cranial head (头) with eyes and mouth, also used to round off everyday nouns like steamed buns (头). | La testa redonda y erguida sobre los hombros (头), empleada como sustantivo y como sufijo cariñoso de alimentos cotidianos (头). | 35 | YK | 頭

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Steamed leavened wheat bread (馒) rounded into plump, smooth domes like little heads (头) makes comforting steamed buns (馒头).
  composite_memory_hook_es: La masa de harina al vapor (馒) moldeada en forma de pequeñas cabecitas redondas (头) compone el panecillo tradicional (馒头).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Legend attributes the invention of mantou (馒头) to Three Kingdoms strategist Zhuge Liang (诸葛亮) during his southern expedition across the Lu River (泸水). Rather than sacrificing human heads to river spirits, he shaped wheat flour loaves into head-like buns.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by neutral tone: 'mán tou' (35-neutral). Rise steadily on 'mán' and pronounce 'tou' lightly without stress.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[5]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    慢 | màn | slow; gradual | Has heart radical 忄 on the left instead of food 饣
    漫 | màn | overflow; unrestrained | Has water radical 氵 on the left instead of food 饣
    买 | mǎi | buy | Has horizontal line at top, distinct from 头
    头 | tóu | head; chief | Has two dots on top and big 大 base
    斗 | dòu | fight; dipper | Different dot placement and central vertical cross
  etymological_cognates[5]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
